### Visual Design System — "Deep Purple"
- tweakcn `Deep Purple` is now the active shared palette across globals, extended tokens, shared primitives, public chrome, and dashboard shell defaults
- Core dark tokens now use plum-black backgrounds with purple accents (`--primary: oklch(0.6083 0.2172 297.1153)`)
- Dashboard default theme is now `violet`, and `THEME_PALETTES.violet` maps to the same Deep Purple palette used by global tokens
- Legacy gold/sage/cobalt hardcodes targeted in app code were removed from the shared theme path

### Typography System
- `app/layout.tsx` keeps `Geist` as the global sans font and mounts it through `--font-sans` with the fallback stack `system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, Segoe UI, sans-serif`
- `app/globals.css` is now the source of truth for the shared type tokens: `--type-display-*`, `--type-h1-*`, `--type-h2-*`, `--type-h3-*`, `--type-h4-*`, `--type-body-lg-*`, `--type-body-*`, `--type-body-sm-*`, `--type-label-*`, and `--type-overline-*`
- The reusable utility classes are `.type-display`, `.type-h1`, `.type-h2`, `.type-h3`, `.type-h4`, `.type-body-lg`, `.type-body`, `.type-body-sm`, `.type-label`, and `.type-overline`
- Home marketing sections now use the shared type classes instead of one-off clamp heading sizes, and dashboard/account/table numerics use `tabular-nums`

### Home Page Structure
- The live home route now keeps a single dashboard product mock inside `Hero.tsx`; the duplicate standalone `DashboardPreview` mount was removed from `HomeContent.tsx`
- `ComparisonSection.tsx` was deleted because its differentiation copy overlapped with the live social-proof/capability sequence
- Home section order now flows: Hero → ProblemStatement → HowItWorks → FeaturesBento → AnalysisDemo → AIFeatures → AudienceSegmentation → PropFirmsExplorer → LiveStatsStrip → SocialProof → Pricing → FAQ → FinalCTA
- `FeaturesBento.tsx` now focuses on core workflow/platform capabilities only; the repeated AI feature grid was removed so `AIFeatures.tsx` remains the single dedicated AI pitch on the page
- The mounted home copy and page metadata now come from locale dictionaries instead of hardcoded strings, with the main source of truth living under `locales/*/landing.ts`

### Dashboard Surface Pattern
- `dashboard-tab-shell.tsx` now acts as a simpler embedded shell instead of adding an extra decorative frame outside the mounted content
- Accounts overview card groups now render as `grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 xl:grid-cols-4 items-stretch gap-4`
- `account-card.tsx` is now a full-height flex column surface with `mt-auto` on the action/footer block so rows stay aligned even when card content lengths differ
- `trade-table-review.tsx` keeps the flatter screenshot-inspired shell and applies `tabular-nums` to financial columns

### Deals Page Spotlight
- `app/[locale]/(landing)/deals/components/deals-experience.tsx` now auto-rotates the “Today’s Biggest & Largest Deals!” spotlight every 5 seconds
- Spotlight rotation pauses on hover and focus so copy buttons, CTAs, and arrows remain easy to use without fighting the timer
- Manual dot indicators were added below the spotlight so users can jump directly to a specific featured deal

